  "scope": "Complete strict Eucharistic Canon of the Rome 1604 Typographia Vaticana Missal from the display title CANON MISSAE and red Sacerdos rubric at the head of printed p. 251 through Per omnia saecula saeculorum, R. Amen and the red Iungit manus beside the chant staff on printed p. 254, before Oremus. Praeceptis salutaribus. Includes the display title, three red headings, all action rubrics and 25 printed crosses under a declared selective reading normalization that shares the letter-form conventions of roman-1570-canon-missae but keeps printed capitalization and punctuation. Excludes the prefaces and Sanctus before p. 251, the Crucifixion plate (archive leaf 0347), the Oremus, Pater noster and everything after it on pp. 254-255, and the retained title and Cum sanctissimum pages, which are identity evidence only. Neither the whole Missal nor diplomatic glyph or chant-pitch completeness is claimed.",
